{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And they journeyed from the mountain of HaShem.</b> Until now they were at Mount Sinai." "<b>A journey of three days.</b> It does not say 'three days' but 'a journey of three days' — that is, from when they journeyed from Sinai until their first encampment, before they ate the quail, was a distance of three days' travel. These are the twentieth of Iyyar, the twenty-first of it, and the twenty-second of it." "<b>And the Ark of the Covenant of HaShem.</b> Some say Moses carried it, as it is written in the Twelve: 'and I sent before you Moses, and Aaron, and Miriam.' But the Ark that Bezalel made was in the middle of the standards."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:18.011870488Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}